  uid=g1:1_66 main
    uid=g1:1_67 StaticText "AGORA / FIELD GUIDE"
    uid=g1:1_68 heading "Owned project verification" level="1"
    uid=g1:1_69 heading "What it is" level="2"
    uid=g1:1_70 StaticText "U01b.B01 adds real, project-owned fixture controls, not a worker or production service. "
    uid=g1:1_71 link "The Node driver" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/scripts/project.mjs.html"
      uid=g1:1_72 StaticText "The Node driver"
    uid=g1:1_73 StaticText ", "
    uid=g1:1_74 link "owned host" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/scripts/project-host.mjs.html"
      uid=g1:1_75 StaticText "owned host"
    uid=g1:1_76 StaticText " and "
    uid=g1:1_77 link "freshness checks" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/scripts/project-checks.mjs.html"
      uid=g1:1_78 StaticText "freshness checks"
    uid=g1:1_79 StaticText " expose one versioned CLI envelope for Agora and an independent Python application. Product readers can start with "
    uid=g1:1_80 link "checking a project" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/checking-a-project.html"
      uid=g1:1_81 StaticText "checking a project"
    uid=g1:1_82 StaticText "."
    uid=g1:1_83 heading "What it does" level="2"
    uid=g1:1_84 StaticText "Doctor checks prerequisites without starting anything. Start allocates an instance and waits for its live identity. Verify drives HTTP and compares literal decisions, persisted database rows and object bytes. Evidence rechecks the instance, head, configuration and artifacts. Stop removes only that instance's live resources while keeping receipts. "
    uid=g1:1_85 link "The manifest" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/agora/project.json.html"
      uid=g1:1_86 StaticText "The manifest"
    uid=g1:1_87 StaticText " binds task lanes 1-4 to a fixed test driver, target, predicates, timeout and cleanup policy. The "
    uid=g1:1_88 link "contract source" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/contracts/schemas/cli.schema.json.html"
      uid=g1:1_89 StaticText "contract source"
    uid=g1:1_90 StaticText " closes reports, instance metadata and journal responses."
    uid=g1:1_91 heading "Why it exists" level="2"
    uid=g1:1_92 StaticText "A successful unit test or screenshot is not proof that a project really ran. A shared database, stolen port or broad process kill can also make another attempt's output look successful. These controls make the subject and cleanup boundary explicit and reject missing, changed or unrelated proof."
    uid=g1:1_93 heading "How it works" level="2"
    uid=g1:1_94 StaticText "HOW IT WORKS · READ IN ORDER"
    uid=g1:1_95 StaticText "Doctor and allocate"
    uid=g1:1_96 StaticText "Check Node 24, PostgreSQL 18 or Python plus its locked validator; allocate a fresh UUID and private root."
    uid=g1:1_97 StaticText "Own the instance"
    uid=g1:1_98 StaticText "The host owns a private control socket, loopback HTTP port, database and object directory; return PID plus process start identity and handle."
    uid=g1:1_99 StaticText "Drive public behavior"
    uid=g1:1_100 StaticText "POST literal same-scope and other-scope commands; GET the committed journal and independently read its stored object bytes."
    uid=g1:1_101 StaticText "Bind proof"
    uid=g1:1_102 StaticText "Record exact head and source/configuration/skill digests, public observations, artifact size and hash; reject drift before reuse."
    uid=g1:1_103 StaticText "Stop narrowly"
    uid=g1:1_104 StaticText "Authenticate the recorded live host and cleanup handle; remove its resources, never the retained evidence or another instance."
    uid=g1:1_105 StaticText "Agora uses its real Hono policy composition and a socket-only PostgreSQL cluster with the existing migrations and non-owner service role. Its verification-only journal is not mounted by the production center. Python uses its own HTTP server, SQLite transactions and the independent "
    uid=g1:1_106 StaticText "jsonschema"
    uid=g1:1_107 StaticText " validator. Each allocates its own object directory. Local filesystem objects are a foundation fixture, not S3 compatibility proof."
    uid=g1:1_108 link "The skill" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/.agents/skills/verify-agora/SKILL.md.html"
      uid=g1:1_109 StaticText "The skill"
    uid=g1:1_110 StaticText " is the literal reproduction recipe. Install the pinned "
    uid=g1:1_111 link "Python requirements" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/packages/verification/fixture/requirements.txt.html"
      uid=g1:1_112 StaticText "Python requirements"
    uid=g1:1_113 StaticText " into "
    uid=g1:1_114 StaticText ".scratch/python"
    uid=g1:1_115 StaticText " and put its "
    uid=g1:1_116 StaticText "bin"
    uid=g1:1_117 StaticText " on PATH. All children receive an environment allowlist; no inherited database URLs, forge tokens or Node hooks are forwarded. Processes still run with the local owner's permissions. This is not a hostile-code sandbox or tamper-proof attestation."
    uid=g1:1_118 StaticText "The registry is "
    uid=g1:1_119 StaticText ".scratch/project/<agora|python>/<UUID>/state.json"
    uid=g1:1_120 StaticText ". It binds checkout, instance, temp root, process identity and cleanup handle. Failed startup logs stay there. A failed cleanup is not removal; retain that registry for recovery. Stop requires the original "
    uid=g1:1_121 StaticText "--handle"
    uid=g1:1_122 StaticText ", not a PID. Evidence lives in the requested repository-contained "
    uid=g1:1_123 StaticText "evidence/"
    uid=g1:1_124 StaticText " or "
    uid=g1:1_125 StaticText ".scratch/"
    uid=g1:1_126 StaticText " directory; symlink escapes refuse. UUID namespaces cannot be reused."
    uid=g1:1_127 heading "Implementation status" level="2"
    uid=g1:1_128 StaticText "In progress pending independent exact-head review."
    uid=g1:1_129 StaticText " The task implementation and five native tests exist, including an isolated guard mutation. No U01b milestone verdict, FG05/FG06, trusted CI, signed general evidence service, browser product UI, production identity or model execution is claimed. The progress atlas changes data only. The design team retains ownership of its replacement visual system; this page uses the existing accessible ordered-flow component."
    uid=g1:1_130 heading "Verification and proof" level="2"
    uid=g1:1_131 link "Behavior tests" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/packages/verification/test/project.test.ts.html"
      uid=g1:1_132 StaticText "Behavior tests"
    uid=g1:1_133 StaticText " exercise both public CLIs, simultaneous instances, foreign cleanup, report disagreement, missing runners, malformed inventory, absent/altered/stale artifacts, skill drift and feature-map deletion. The guard assertion passes normally and turns red when only the artifact-byte check is disabled in an isolated copy. "
    uid=g1:1_134 link "The initial intended-assertion red" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/source/evidence/U01b/agora-s1-isolate-development/assertion-red.log.html"
      uid=g1:1_135 StaticText "The initial intended-assertion red"
    uid=g1:1_136 StaticText " follows a callable baseline. Full task receipts, including failed attempts, are retained under "
    uid=g1:1_137 StaticText "evidence/U01b/agora-s1-isolate-development/"
    uid=g1:1_138 StaticText "; their headers, not a status badge, name exact tested revisions. The "
    uid=g1:1_139 link "CLI reference" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/cli.html#owned-project-controls"
      uid=g1:1_140 StaticText "CLI reference"
    uid=g1:1_141 StaticText " distinguishes task proof from unimplemented milestone lanes."
    uid=g1:1_142 link "Improve this page" url="http://127.0.0.1:43261/authoring.html"
      uid=g1:1_143 StaticText "Improve this page"
    uid=g1:1_144 StaticText "Documentation is part of implementation."
